## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design scalable, privacy-aware audit pipelines for multi-tenant clusters, balancing compliance with operational overhead.

## Key Concepts
- Kubernetes Audit Logs
- Webhook backends & mutating webhooks
- Per-tenant identity normalization
- Privacy redaction & data retention
- Real-time anomaly detection & alerting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-processor: route audit events to tenant-scoped store
function routeEvent(evt){
  const tenant = evt.user.tenant;
  store.append(tenant, evt);
  if (detectAnomaly(evt, tenant)) alert(tenant, evt);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test for false positives at scale?
- Which storage/processing stack would you choose for 1k+ tenants and why?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to apply attestation to WASM plugins in edge/k8s environments, a realistic gap beyond container images.

## Key Concepts

- WASM module signing with cosign
- Rekor attestations for wasm artifacts
- Runtime verification in a restricted loader
- Policy enforcement with Kyverno/OPA
- Edge CI/CD integration with registry labels

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo loader verification
async function verifyAndLoad(wasmName) {
  const att = await fetch(`https://rekor.example/attestations/${wasmName}`);
  if (!att?.valid) throw new Error('Attestation missing or invalid');
  // Load WASM module
  return await WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming(fetch(wasmName));
}
```
